No, protein Q8N4A0 (Polypeptide N-acetylgalactosaminyltransferase 4, encoded by *GALNT4*) does not have more than 636 residues. 

While the primary record field reports a length of 694 amino acids, deterministic verification against the sequence record (AlphaFold DB / UniProt sequence) shows the actual length is **578** residues (with a mass of 66,665.07 Da rather than the reported 79,171 Da).

{"answer": "no", "concerns": ["The record reports a length of 694 amino acids and mass of 79,171 Da, which mismatches the verified sequence length of 578 amino acids and mass of 66,665.07 Da."]}

